Fillets: a convex rounding whose chain runs up into the mitre where two
earlier convex roundings tighter than its ball meet, closed by the torus of
their ball (mitcad#1414).

The case: a wedge (two planes A and B at 90 degrees) standing on a plate,
its foot edges rounded with 1.5 and its top edges with rk = 2.5; its
vertical edge, a line, is then rounded with R = 3. The top roundings are
cylinders tangent to A and B along their edges at the vertical edge's top
V; they meet in a mitre Em from V (to which it is tangent) up to W on the
top T. The vertical edge's tangent chain takes both mitres (at the foot and
at the top). Over the top mitre the ball of R would have to touch both
cylinders of rk from inside: its centre lies rk - R < 0 from their axes,
there is no section at all, and OCCT's walk failed at once
(ChFiDS_WalkingFailure), on the replayed and on the stored body.

The construction is the one the bodies stored in the files have: the
rounding along the vertical edge (a cylinder between A and B) stops at V's
section; the ball of rk rolls between the rounding's end and T, a torus
about the rounding's axis (major radius R - rk, minor rk, its tube circle
rk inside T), from the section of one top rounding (its meridian through
the rounding's contact with A) to the other's. The top roundings are cut
along those sections, T along the torus's contact (a circle of radius
R - rk), and the mitre and the strips of the top roundings beside it go.
On the reported design's stored body after the rounding the corner is
exactly that torus (12.9017 mm2, major radius 0.5, minor 2.5).

- ChFi3d_ConvexMitre (new): whether the edge Em at the end of a chain past
  its edge Ex is such a mitre: Ex a line between the planes A and B, Em
  between two cylinders KA and KB of one radius rk below R, KA tangent to
  A and KB to B along their edges through V, both to the plane T along
  their edges through Em's other vertex W, T square to Ex, the cylinders'
  axes square to Ex, rk inside their planes and T and through the torus's
  tube circle (radius R - rk about the ball's axis between A and B, rk
  inside T, at V's height).
- ChFi3d_Builder::SplitAtConvexMitres (new, at the start of Compute, after
  SplitAtTightConcaveArcs): a convex open contour of constant radius whose
  first or last edge is such a mitre leaves it out; the contour ends at V
  with the status ChFiDS_Tangent.
- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformConvexMitreCorners (new, after
  PerformTightConcaveCorners, before the corners at vertices), for each
  such end: the stripe ends on the arc of radius R about the ball's axis
  in V's section, from PA on A to PB on B (its contacts' ends, on the
  edges A and B share with KA and KB, the parts towards V taken away);
  the torus is a corner stripe on the stripe's blend (that arc) and T
  (the circle from QA to QB, on the edges KA and KB share with T, the
  parts towards W taken away), from KA's meridian PA-QA to KB's PB-QB;
  KA and KB are cut along the meridians (G1 with the torus), the parts
  towards the mitre taken away; the torus is generated from the mitre's
  edge. Where a corner cannot be built the fillet fails as before.
- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformTightCorners leaves such ends to it.

